      "date": "2026-11-24 14:39:19.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nMostly good. The claim/release logic around cl_sync_transno looks correct, including the send-failure, timeout and eviction paths. There is one question inline about objects skipped while a sync is in flight; if that gap is intended, no re-spin is needed. Nothing exercises the reclaim sync rate. If it is practical, a test that counts ost_sync in osc.*.stats for a memcg-limited writer would help keep this from regressing.",
